@startuml
title Queue Management Platform — Day Start Sequence

participant "Day Start Scheduler" as Scheduler
participant "Application Service" as App
participant "ServiceProvider" as Provider
participant "Ticket Repository" as Tickets
participant "Queue" as Queue
participant "Ticket" as Ticket

Scheduler -> App : Activate appointments for today

App -> Provider : Check physical presence

alt Provider absent

    Provider --> App : Absent
    App --> Scheduler : Activation skipped

else Provider present

    Provider --> App : Present

    App -> Tickets : Find SCHEDULED tickets for today
    Tickets --> App : Scheduled tickets

    App -> Queue : Begin queue-protected activation

    App -> Queue : Get existing WAITING tickets
    Queue --> App : Existing queue order

    note right of Queue
    Existing WAITING tickets preserve their exact current positions within their priority groups.
    end note

    App -> App : Sort SCHEDULED tickets\nby createdAt ASC, then Ticket.id ASC

    loop For each SCHEDULED ticket

        App -> Ticket : SCHEDULED → WAITING

        alt isPriority = true

            App -> Queue : Insert after existing Priority group

        else isPriority = false

            App -> Queue : Insert after existing Normal group

        end

        Queue -> Queue : Assign operational position
        Queue --> App : Position assigned

    end

    App -> Queue : Commit activation transaction

    note right of App
    Appointment type does not imply priority.
    isPriority determines the target group.

    Within each priority group, newly activated appointments preserve createdAt ASC, then Ticket.id ASC.

    Existing WAITING tickets are never displaced.

    Morning activation does not start service.
    First service requires an explicit provider action.
    end note

    App --> Scheduler : Activation completed

end

@enduml